# Top-level heading

Some prose with a paragraph and a list.

### Skipped a level deliberately

This file uses ATX headings. When parsed as raw HTML, `# Top-level heading`
is text content inside a `<body>` shell — heading-hierarchy never sees it.
When parsed as markdown-html-residue, the harness strips the ATX residue
the same way `.md` and `.markdown` already do, and the rule downgrades
its evidence model accordingly.
